{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.ParticleInteractions.operator_selection_lp","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.operator_selection_lp","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.Finset.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Ring.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Fintype.Fin","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Ring.Finset","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.BigOperators.Group.Finset","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":38,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.operator_selection_lp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.operator_selection_lp","kind":"theorem","line":727,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/operator_selection_lp.lean#L727-L747","doc":"**Operator selection LP** ([`prop:operator-selection-lp`]).\n\n`x*` is feasible, is the minimum-objective feasible point, and the\ndual variable `y₀*` certifies optimality via strong duality\n`objective x* = n_target · y₀*`. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:operator-selection-lp","label":"prop:operator-selection-lp","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/operator-selection-lp.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.OperatorSelectionLpContext.complementary_slackness_x_star","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.OperatorSelectionLpContext.complementary_slackness_x_star","kind":"theorem","line":718,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/operator_selection_lp.lean#L718-L723","doc":"Complementary slackness holds at `x*`, as a consequence of the\nclass's `zero_gap` field.  This is the per-index statement a\nsubstrate evaluation can check directly. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.OperatorSelectionLpContext.tightening_preserves_optimum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.OperatorSelectionLpContext.tightening_preserves_optimum","kind":"theorem","line":688,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/operator_selection_lp.lean#L688-L716","doc":"**A tightening buys nothing if the optimum survives it.**\n\n`Tighter` is an arbitrary refinement of `IsFeasible` — a PSD lift, a\nLasserre moment relaxation, extra cuts, anything at all.  The only\nhypotheses are that it *is* a refinement (`hsub`) and that `x*` still\nsatisfies it (`hstar`).  Then `x*` is optimal for the tightened\nprogram too, at the same value.\n\nThis is what settles the third candidate in bean `qou/ndsa`.  The\nmoment lift in `computations/sdp_moment_lift.py` keeps `Gx ≥ 0` and\nadds `M ⪰ 0`, `X ⪰ 0`, `tr(GX) ≥ 0`, so `hsub` holds by inspection.\nAnd `x*` lifts: take the rank-one moment matrix `X = x*x*ᵀ`, which is\nPSD by construction and satisfies `tr(GX) = x*ᵀ(Gx*) = 0` because\n`Gx* = 0` — every Frobenius constraint is tight at the radical\noptimum.  So `hstar` holds too, and the SDP's optimal value is the\nLP's.\n\nThe lesson is not about semidefinite programming.  A tightening can\nonly help when it *cuts off* the incumbent optimum, and this one\ncannot: `x*` is the point where all the constraints already hold with\nequality. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.OperatorSelectionLpContext.zero_gap_iff_complementary_slackness","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.OperatorSelectionLpContext.zero_gap_iff_complementary_slackness","kind":"theorem","line":665,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/operator_selection_lp.lean#L665-L686","doc":"**Complementary slackness is the whole content of the zero gap.**\n\nFor a feasible `x`, attaining the dual bound is *equivalent* to the\nper-index condition `sᵢ (Gx)ᵢ = 0` for every `i`: each Frobenius\nconstraint is either inactive (`sᵢ = 0`) or tight (`(Gx)ᵢ = 0`).\n\nThis is the reduction that makes the certificate checkable.  The\nglobal identity `Σⱼ tⱼxⱼ = n_target · y₀*` is one equation in the\nwhole data; the right-hand side is `d` independent scalar equations,\neach of which a symbolic evaluation can discharge index by index. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.OperatorSelectionLpContext.slackPairing_eq_zero_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.OperatorSelectionLpContext.slackPairing_eq_zero_iff","kind":"theorem","line":656,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/operator_selection_lp.lean#L656-L663","doc":"The slack pairing vanishes exactly when every index contributes\nzero — a sum of non-negative terms is zero iff each term is. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.OperatorSelectionLpContext.dual_bound_le_objective","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.OperatorSelectionLpContext.dual_bound_le_objective","kind":"theorem","line":649,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/operator_selection_lp.lean#L649-L654","doc":"**Weak duality.** Every feasible point's objective is bounded below\nby the dual value `n_target · y₀*`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.OperatorSelectionLpContext.slackPairing_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.OperatorSelectionLpContext.slackPairing_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":643,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/operator_selection_lp.lean#L643-L647","doc":"The slack pairing is non-negative on feasible points: `sᵢ ≥ 0` by\ndual feasibility and `(Gx)ᵢ ≥ 0` by primal feasibility. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.OperatorSelectionLpContext.objective_eq_dual_add_slackPairing","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.OperatorSelectionLpContext.objective_eq_dual_add_slackPairing","kind":"theorem","line":636,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/operator_selection_lp.lean#L636-L641","doc":"Dual decomposition, specialised to the class: `objective x` is the\ndual bound plus the slack pairing.  Only the net constraint is\nused, not Frobenius positivity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.OperatorSelectionLpContext.slackPairing","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.OperatorSelectionLpContext.slackPairing","kind":"def","line":630,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/operator_selection_lp.lean#L630-L634","doc":"The **slack pairing** `Σᵢ sᵢ (Gx)ᵢ` — the amount by which a\nfeasible point's objective exceeds the dual bound. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.OperatorSelectionLpContext.objective","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.OperatorSelectionLpContext.objective","kind":"def","line":626,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/operator_selection_lp.lean#L626-L628","doc":"The objective value `Σᵢ tᵢ xᵢ` of a candidate `x`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.OperatorSelectionLpContext.IsFeasible","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.OperatorSelectionLpContext.IsFeasible","kind":"def","line":577,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/operator_selection_lp.lean#L577-L624","doc":"A vector `x : Fin d → R` is LP-feasible: it satisfies the net\nconstraint and Frobenius positivity.  The box `xᵢ ≥ -M` is dropped.\n\n**Why dropping it is sound, and why the old reason was the wrong\none.**  This docstring used to say the box was \"absorbed into the\nexistence of a large `M`\" and call the other two \"the two binding\nconstraints\".  That is not what happens.  In the committed solve\n(`computations/a-K-via-lp-dual-hecke-basis.witness.json`, both atoms)\n\n    x*₀ = -1000000.0 = -M   exactly ,\n\nso the box at index `0` is **active** at the solver's optimum.  Bean\n`qou/0tjt` concluded \"the box is non-binding at `x*`\" and this file\ndropped it on that basis; the statement is true of the radical\noptimum `x* = c·v` that `0tjt` reasoned about and false of the\nvertex the solver returned.  The LP has many optima and they differ\non this.\n\nDropping the box does not depend on either.  Two reasons, both\nindependent of where the optimum sits:\n\n1. **The drop only enlarges `IsFeasible`.**  Every theorem below is\n   either \"`x*` satisfies these two constraints\" — unaffected — or\n   \"`x*` is optimal among all feasible points\" / a lower bound over\n   all feasible points, which is *strengthened* by admitting more\n   points.  A boxed optimum is a relaxed-feasible point, so nothing\n   here can be true of the relaxation and false of the box.\n2. **The certificate, not the box, is what bounds the program.**\n   `dual_bound_le_objective` uses the net constraint, Frobenius\n   positivity and `s ≥ 0`, and nothing else.  The box exists in the\n   narrative to make the polyhedron bounded; here the dual bound\n   already does that, so the box is not load-bearing for any\n   conclusion.\n\nWhat *is* true of the witness, and is the right form of `0tjt`'s\nclaim: the box **multipliers** vanish, which is what makes the\nnarrative's `≤` dual tight and the equality `dual_feasible` correct.\nWith `y = e₀` and `y₀ = 0`, `μⱼ = tⱼ - y₀ - Σᵢ Gⱼᵢ yᵢ = tⱼ - Gⱼ₀ = 0`\nfor every `j`, because `t` is row `0` of `G` and `G` is symmetric.\nSo index `0` is an active constraint with a zero multiplier —\nprimal degeneracy at a box vertex, not a constraint that binds in\nthe dual sense.  Note this holds for the structural reason\n`t = G₀·`, not because `M` was chosen large.\n\nThis is a genuine predicate on the data, not a projected field. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.OperatorSelectionLpContext.ofRadical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.OperatorSelectionLpContext.ofRadical","kind":"def","line":533,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/operator_selection_lp.lean#L533-L570","doc":"**The radical direction, scaled to meet the net constraint, is an\n    optimum — and the optimal value is zero.**\n\nTake `x* = c·v` with `c·Σⱼvⱼ = n_target`.  Then `Gx* = 0`, so every\nFrobenius constraint is *tight*, complementary slackness is trivial,\nand the objective vanishes.\n\nThe inputs are three facts about the data and nothing else:\n\n- `ht` — the cost vector is row `i₀` of `G` (automatic for a trace\n  form with `b_{i₀} = 1`),\n- `hv` — `v` is a right radical direction of `G`,\n- `hc` — `c` scales `v` onto the net constraint (solvable exactly when\n  `Σⱼvⱼ ≠ 0`, the same non-degeneracy `y_0_eq_zero_of_radical` needs).\n\nRead together with that theorem this is the whole story for a\ndegenerate trace form: `y₀ = 0` is forced, the optimum is `0`, and it\nis attained on the radical — the direction the trace form cannot see. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.OperatorSelectionLpContext.ofCertificate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.OperatorSelectionLpContext.ofCertificate","kind":"def","line":500,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/operator_selection_lp.lean#L500-L531","doc":"**Build a context from a dual certificate and a primal point.**\n\nThis is the constructor an instantiation should use.  It takes only\nfacts that are *checkable on concrete data* — slack signs, the dual\nequation, the net constraint, Frobenius positivity, and per-index\ncomplementary slackness — and derives `zero_gap` rather than\ndemanding it.\n\nThat the gap is derived, not supplied, is the point: `zero_gap` is the\none field that looks like the block's own conclusion, and building it\nby hand is where a self-assuming instance would creep back in. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.OperatorSelectionLpContext.zero_gap","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.OperatorSelectionLpContext.zero_gap","kind":"theorem","line":498,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/operator_selection_lp.lean#L498-L498","doc":"Zero duality gap at `x*`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.OperatorSelectionLpContext.x_star_feasible","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.OperatorSelectionLpContext.x_star_feasible","kind":"theorem","line":494,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/operator_selection_lp.lean#L494-L494","doc":"`x*` is primal feasible. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.OperatorSelectionLpContext.dual_feasible","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.OperatorSelectionLpContext.dual_feasible","kind":"theorem","line":492,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/operator_selection_lp.lean#L492-L492","doc":"Dual feasibility: `tⱼ = y₀ + Σᵢ sᵢ Gᵢⱼ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.OperatorSelectionLpContext.s_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.OperatorSelectionLpContext.s_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":490,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/operator_selection_lp.lean#L490-L490","doc":"Dual feasibility: the slacks are non-negative. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.OperatorSelectionLpContext.s","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.OperatorSelectionLpContext.s","kind":"def","line":488,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/operator_selection_lp.lean#L488-L488","doc":"Dual slack for the Frobenius-positivity constraints. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.OperatorSelectionLpContext.y_0_star","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.OperatorSelectionLpContext.y_0_star","kind":"def","line":486,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/operator_selection_lp.lean#L486-L486","doc":"The Markov-trace dual variable `y₀* : R`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.OperatorSelectionLpContext.x_star","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.OperatorSelectionLpContext.x_star","kind":"def","line":484,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/operator_selection_lp.lean#L484-L484","doc":"The candidate primal point `x* : Fin d → R`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.OperatorSelectionLpContext.G","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.OperatorSelectionLpContext.G","kind":"def","line":482,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/operator_selection_lp.lean#L482-L482","doc":"The Frobenius Gram matrix `G : Fin d → Fin d → R`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.OperatorSelectionLpContext.t","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.OperatorSelectionLpContext.t","kind":"def","line":480,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/operator_selection_lp.lean#L480-L480","doc":"The Markov-trace cost coefficients `t : Fin d → R`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.OperatorSelectionLpContext.n_target","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.OperatorSelectionLpContext.n_target","kind":"def","line":478,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/operator_selection_lp.lean#L478-L478","doc":"The target net value `n_target`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.OperatorSelectionLpContext.d","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.OperatorSelectionLpContext.d","kind":"def","line":476,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/operator_selection_lp.lean#L476-L476","doc":"The basis cardinality `d = n!`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.OperatorSelectionLpContext.n","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.OperatorSelectionLpContext.n","kind":"def","line":474,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/operator_selection_lp.lean#L474-L474","doc":"The strand number `n ≥ 2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.OperatorSelectionLpContext.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.OperatorSelectionLpContext.mk","kind":"ctor","line":471,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/operator_selection_lp.lean#L471-L471","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.OperatorSelectionLpContext","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.OperatorSelectionLpContext","kind":"class","line":467,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/operator_selection_lp.lean#L467-L498","doc":"Data of the operator-selection LP: the cost vector `t`, the\nFrobenius Gram matrix `G`, the target net value `n_target`, a\ncandidate primal point `x*`, and the net-constraint dual variable\n`y₀*`.  These are *inputs*; nothing here asserts the conclusion. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.demand_perp_radical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.demand_perp_radical","kind":"theorem","line":442,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/operator_selection_lp.lean#L442-L463","doc":"**A demand profile has to be orthogonal to the radical to be\n    feasible at all.**\n\nIf `v` is a *left* radical direction then `Gx = u` forces `⟨u,v⟩ = 0`.\nSo a knot-derived `u` is not free: it must satisfy this linear\ncondition before the program has any feasible point.  (For a symmetric\nGram the left and right radicals coincide, so this is the same `v` as\neverywhere else here.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.objective_constant_on_demand_fibre","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.objective_constant_on_demand_fibre","kind":"theorem","line":430,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/operator_selection_lp.lean#L430-L439","doc":"Two points with the same demand score the same — the objective is\nconstant on each fibre of `x ↦ Gx`, so \"optimal\" is vacuous. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.objective_eq_demand_coord","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.objective_eq_demand_coord","kind":"theorem","line":405,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/operator_selection_lp.lean#L405-L427","doc":"**Fixing `Gx` fixes the objective.**\n\nThe *equality*-constrained variant of the program — `min t·x` subject\nto `1·x = n_target` and `Gx = u` — has nothing to optimise when the\ncost vector is row `i₀` of `G`:\n\n    t·x = Σⱼ G_{i₀j}xⱼ = (Gx)_{i₀} = u_{i₀} .\n\nEvery feasible point scores the same, and the score is a coordinate of\nthe demand vector the caller passed in.  Making `u` depend on a knot\ntherefore makes the \"optimum\" depend on the knot only by reading one\ncomponent of its own input back out.\n\nBean `qou/ndsa` names this formulation as the cheapest candidate for\nbreaking the confinement LP's homogeneity.  This is why it does not. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.y_0_eq_zero_of_radical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.y_0_eq_zero_of_radical","kind":"theorem","line":387,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/operator_selection_lp.lean#L387-L402","doc":"The trace-form instance of the above: when the cost vector is row\n`i₀` of `G`, orthogonality to the radical is automatic, since\n`Σⱼ tⱼvⱼ = Σⱼ G_{i₀j}vⱼ = 0` is just `hv` at `i₀`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.y_0_eq_zero_of_cost_perp_radical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.y_0_eq_zero_of_cost_perp_radical","kind":"theorem","line":340,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/operator_selection_lp.lean#L340-L384","doc":"**The radical of the form forces the dual variable to vanish.**\n\nThree hypotheses, and *none of them says where the Gram came from*:\n\n- `hv` — `v` is a right radical direction, `∀ i, Σⱼ Gᵢⱼvⱼ = 0`;\n- `htv` — the cost vector is orthogonal to it, `Σⱼ tⱼvⱼ = 0`;\n- `hone` — `Σⱼ vⱼ ≠ 0`.\n\nThen *every* dual-feasible `y₀` is `0`.\n\nThe dual objective is `n_target · y₀`, so this says the LP's value is\nidentically zero however `n_target` is chosen, and `y₀` is **not** a\nshadow price of the net constraint: it cannot respond to the constraint\nit is supposed to price.\n\nNote how little is assumed.  No symmetry of `G`, no non-negativity of\nthe slacks, no primal feasibility, no optimality.  Degeneracy is a\nproperty of the cost vector and the form alone — which is why it\ncannot be repaired by choosing a better `x*`, and (bean `qou/ndsa`)\nwhy it cannot be repaired by rebuilding `G` either: see\n`y_0_eq_zero_of_radical` below for the version whose `htv` comes for\nfree.\n\nThe `omit` above is load-bearing documentation, not tidying: this\nstatement holds over any commutative ring without zero divisors, with\nno order in sight. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.y_0_eq_zero_of_contribution_perp_radical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.y_0_eq_zero_of_contribution_perp_radical","kind":"theorem","line":298,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/operator_selection_lp.lean#L298-L337","doc":"**The degeneracy criterion, in the only form that is really needed.**\n\nStrip everything away and dual feasibility for the `x`-block of *any*\nconic program has the shape\n\n    tⱼ = y₀ + cⱼ\n\nwhere `c` is whatever the constraints contribute.  For a linear\nprogram `cⱼ = Σᵢ sᵢGᵢⱼ`; for an SDP with lift `M₀ + Σₖ xₖMₖ ⪰ 0` and\ndual `Z ⪰ 0` it is `cⱼ = ⟨Z, Mⱼ⟩`; for a moment relaxation it picks up\nthe moment block as well.\n\nWhatever it is, `y₀ = 0` follows as soon as the contribution is\northogonal to `v`.  So the question to ask of any proposed\nreformulation is exactly one thing:\n\n> **does the constraint map annihilate the radical?**\n\nIf it does, the reformulation is degenerate before it is solved.  For\nthe LP that is `Gv = 0`; for a dense PSD lift it is `Σⱼ vⱼMⱼ = 0`.\nBean `qou/ndsa`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.dualCertificateExists_of_cost_eq_gram_row","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.dualCertificateExists_of_cost_eq_gram_row","kind":"theorem","line":278,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/operator_selection_lp.lean#L278-L295","doc":"**A cost vector that is a row of the Gram matrix certifies itself.**\n\nFor a *trace form* this hypothesis is not an assumption but an\nidentity: `tᵢ = tr(bᵢ) = tr(b_{i₀}·bᵢ) = G_{i₀ i}` whenever the basis\ncontains the identity element `b_{i₀} = 1`.  The certificate is then\n`y₀ = 0`, `s = e_{i₀}`.\n\nSo certificate *existence* is never the obstruction for a trace-form\nLP.  But look at what the certificate bounds: it gives\n`Σⱼ tⱼxⱼ ≥ 0` using the constraint `(Gx)_{i₀} ≥ 0`, and `(Gx)_{i₀}`\n*is* `Σⱼ tⱼxⱼ`.  The objective is bounded below by one of its own\nconstraints, and the bound is a tautology. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.dualCertificateExists_of_left_inverse","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.dualCertificateExists_of_left_inverse","kind":"theorem","line":231,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/operator_selection_lp.lean#L231-L270","doc":"**Reduction to a one-parameter sign condition.**\n\nIf `K` is a left inverse of `G` — `Σᵢ K k i · G i j = δₖⱼ` — then the\ndual equation `t = y₀·𝟙 + sᵀG` determines `s` outright:\n\n    s i = Σₖ (t k − y₀) · K k i .\n\nSo a certificate exists as soon as *some single scalar* `y₀` makes all\n`d` of those entries non-negative.  A `d`-dimensional feasibility\nproblem collapses to a search over one parameter.\n\nThis is the statement the symbolic stage answers: invert `G` over\n`ℚ(q)`, form `s(y₀)`, and ask for which `y₀` every entry is `≥ 0`.\nNote the hypothesis is a *given* left inverse, not `G⁻¹` — so no\ninvertibility API, no determinant, and the symbolic stage supplies\n`K` explicitly and checks `hK` by multiplication. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.DualCertificateExists","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.DualCertificateExists","kind":"def","line":219,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/operator_selection_lp.lean#L219-L229","doc":"A **dual certificate** for cost vector `t` and Gram matrix `G`: a\n    scalar `y₀` together with non-negative slacks `s` satisfying\n    `t = y₀·𝟙 + sᵀG`.\n\nExistence is *not* automatic.  It asks whether `t` lies in the cone\n`{y₀·𝟙 + sᵀG : y₀ ∈ R, s ≥ 0}` — `d` equations in `d+1` unknowns with\na sign constraint, a genuine Farkas-type question about the substrate\ndata.  Bean `qou/k4f8`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.zero_gap_of_complementary_slackness","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.zero_gap_of_complementary_slackness","kind":"theorem","line":195,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/operator_selection_lp.lean#L195-L211","doc":"**Certificate builder.** Over raw LP data, the zero-gap identity\n    follows from dual feasibility, the net constraint, and *per-index*\n    complementary slackness `sᵢ (Gx*)ᵢ = 0`.\n\nThis is the form an instantiation needs.  `zero_gap` is a *field* of\n`OperatorSelectionLpContext`, so a lemma assuming the class cannot be\nused to supply it; this one assumes only the data.  Checking `d`\nscalar products vanish is decidable on concrete symbolic `t`, `G`,\n`x*`, whereas the global sum identity is not. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.sum_cost_mul_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.sum_cost_mul_eq","kind":"theorem","line":167,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/operator_selection_lp.lean#L167-L193","doc":"**Dual decomposition** of the objective, over raw LP data.\n\nFor any `x` meeting the net constraint, dual feasibility rewrites the\nobjective as the dual bound plus the *slack pairing* `Σᵢ sᵢ (Gx)ᵢ`:\n\n    Σⱼ tⱼ xⱼ = y₀ · n_target + Σᵢ sᵢ (Gx)ᵢ .\n\nThis is pure algebra — no order on `R` is used, and neither `sᵢ ≥ 0`\nnor `(Gx)ᵢ ≥ 0` is assumed.  Both the optimality bound and the\ncomplementary-slackness equivalence below are corollaries of this one\nidentity. ","signatureChunk":0}]}